  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main" data-i18n="nav.skip">Skip to content</a>

    <header class="site-header">
      <div class="site-header-inner">
        <a class="brand" href="/">
          <img src="/assets/favicon-32.png" alt="">
          <span>Easy Fox Games</span>
        </a>
        <div class="lang-picker">
          <button class="lang-picker-btn" type="button" aria-haspopup="listbox" aria-expanded="false">
            <span id="lang-current-label">English</span>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M2.5 4.5L6 8L9.5 4.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            </svg>
          </button>
          <ul class="lang-menu" id="lang-menu" role="listbox" aria-label="Language"></ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main id="main">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="page-head">
          <p class="page-kicker" data-i18n="head.kicker">AI Transparency</p>
          <h1 class="page-title" data-i18n="head.title">How this game uses AI</h1>
          <p class="page-lede" data-i18n="head.lede">Teach My Little Sister How to Drive talks with you in real time. To make that work, your voice is sent to external AI services while a conversation is running. This page lists which services we use, when each one is used, what is sent to them, and what each provider does with it.</p>
          <p class="updated" data-i18n="head.updated">Last updated: 27 August 2026</p>
        </div>

        <section class="block" aria-labelledby="region-title">
          <h2 class="block-title" id="region-title" data-i18n="region.title">Choose your region</h2>
          <p class="block-intro" data-i18n="region.intro">We use different providers depending on where the game runs. Pick the region that applies to you.</p>
          <nav class="region-switch" aria-label="Region">
            <a href="/tsd/ai/privacy/gl" aria-current="page" data-i18n="region.global">Global</a>
            <a href="/tsd/ai/privacy/cn" data-i18n="region.china">Chinese mainland</a>
          </nav>
          <p class="region-note" data-i18n="region.note">You are reading the global version. In the Chinese mainland the game uses Alibaba Cloud and BytePlus services instead, under different terms.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="block" aria-labelledby="svc-title">
          <h2 class="block-title" id="svc-title" data-i18n="svc.title">Services we use</h2>
          <p class="block-intro" data-i18n="svc.intro">Two providers, three models. Google normally answers you. The OpenAI models take over when the first choice is too slow or cannot be reached, so the conversation does not break in the middle of a drive.</p>

          <div class="model-grid">
            <article class="model-card">
              <span class="model-role primary" data-i18n="role.primary">Primary</span>
              <p class="model-id">gemini-2.5-flash</p>
              <p class="model-provider" data-i18n="p.google">Google — Vertex AI</p>
              <dl class="model-facts">
                <dt data-i18n="fact.handles">What it handles</dt>
                <dd data-i18n="m1.handles">Listening to what you say and speaking the in-game reply back to you.</dd>
                <dt data-i18n="fact.processed">Processed by</dt>
                <dd data-i18n="m1.processed">Google, on Vertex AI.</dd>
              </dl>
            </article>

            <article class="model-card">
              <span class="model-role fallback" data-i18n="role.fallback1">Fallback 1</span>
              <p class="model-id">ChatGPT Realtime Mini 2.1</p>
              <p class="model-provider" data-i18n="p.openai">OpenAI — Realtime API</p>
              <dl class="model-facts">
                <dt data-i18n="fact.handles">What it handles</dt>
                <dd data-i18n="m2.handles">The same conversation, taken over when the primary service is slow or unreachable.</dd>
                <dt data-i18n="fact.processed">Processed by</dt>
                <dd data-i18n="m2.processed">OpenAI, through the Realtime API.</dd>
              </dl>
            </article>

            <article class="model-card">
              <span class="model-role fallback" data-i18n="role.fallback2">Fallback 2</span>
              <p class="model-id">ChatGPT Realtime Mini</p>
              <p class="model-provider" data-i18n="p.openai">OpenAI — Realtime API</p>
              <dl class="model-facts">
                <dt data-i18n="fact.handles">What it handles</dt>
                <dd data-i18n="m3.handles">The last step, used if the first fallback fails as well.</dd>
                <dt data-i18n="fact.processed">Processed by</dt>
                <dd data-i18n="m3.processed">OpenAI, through the Realtime API.</dd>
              </dl>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="block" aria-labelledby="flow-title">
          <h2 class="block-title" id="flow-title" data-i18n="flow.title">How the game connects</h2>
          <p class="block-intro" data-i18n="flow.intro">The choice is made inside the game. A selector built into the game watches the connection, moves to the next service when the current one is too slow or cannot be reached, and retries the higher-priority service at regular intervals.</p>

          <div class="diagram">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 900 450" role="img" aria-labelledby="diagram-title diagram-desc">
              <title id="diagram-title" data-i18n="diagram.title">How the game connects to AI services</title>
              <desc id="diagram-desc" data-i18n="diagram.desc">The game and its model selector run on your device. Our server only confirms that you own the game and returns a short-lived token; no voice passes through it. The game then streams your voice directly to gemini-2.5-flash on Vertex AI, falling back to ChatGPT Realtime Mini 2.1 and then ChatGPT Realtime Mini when a connection is slow or fails, and retrying the higher-priority service at regular intervals.</desc>

              <defs>
                <marker id="ah" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                  <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="#5c5c72"/>
                </marker>
                <marker id="ah-green" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                  <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="#2e7d32"/>
                </marker>
              </defs>

              <!-- everything inside this boundary runs on the player's device -->
              <rect x="16" y="40" width="380" height="250" rx="20" fill="#fbfcff" stroke="#1e88e5" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="8 6"/>
              <text class="d-group" x="206" y="64" text-anchor="middle" data-i18n="d.device">Your device</text>

              <rect x="48" y="82" width="316" height="60" rx="12" fill="#eef4ff" stroke="#1e88e5" stroke-width="2"/>
              <text class="d-label" x="206" y="106" text-anchor="middle" data-i18n="d.client">Game</text>
              <text class="d-sub" x="206" y="126" text-anchor="middle" data-i18n="d.client.sub">Your voice and game state</text>

              <line x1="206" y1="142" x2="206" y2="178" stroke="#5c5c72" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#ah)"/>

              <rect x="48" y="182" width="316" height="96" rx="12" fill="#fff3e0" stroke="#f57c00" stroke-width="2"/>
              <text class="d-label" x="206" y="214" text-anchor="middle" data-i18n="d.router">Model selector</text>
              <text class="d-sub" x="206" y="236" text-anchor="middle" data-i18n="d.router.sub">Watches the connection</text>
              <text class="d-sub" x="206" y="254" text-anchor="middle" data-i18n="d.router.sub2">and switches service</text>

              <!-- our server: entitlement check only, never audio -->
              <rect x="48" y="345" width="316" height="80" rx="12" fill="#f4f6fb" stroke="#5c5c72" stroke-width="2"/>
              <text class="d-label" x="206" y="373" text-anchor="middle" data-i18n="d.server">Easy Fox server</text>
              <text class="d-sub" x="206" y="393" text-anchor="middle" data-i18n="d.server.sub">Confirms you own the game</text>
              <text class="d-sub" x="206" y="411" text-anchor="middle" data-i18n="d.server.sub2">and returns a temporary token</text>

              <line x1="206" y1="341" x2="206" y2="296" stroke="#5c5c72" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#ah)"/>
              <text class="d-edge" x="218" y="322" text-anchor="start" fill="#5c5c72" data-i18n="d.token">token only — no voice</text>

              <!-- calls that leave the device carrying voice -->
              <text class="d-group" x="655" y="22" text-anchor="middle" data-i18n="d.providers">Model providers — external</text>

              <path d="M364,205 C450,205 460,76 512,76" fill="none" stroke="#2e7d32" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#ah-green)"/>
              <text class="d-edge" x="458" y="120" text-anchor="middle" fill="#2e7d32" data-i18n="d.edge.default">default</text>

              <path d="M364,230 C450,230 460,216 512,216" fill="none" stroke="#5c5c72" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="6 4" marker-end="url(#ah)"/>
              <text class="d-edge" x="458" y="208" text-anchor="middle" fill="#b25000" data-i18n="d.edge.slow1">slow or failing</text>

              <path d="M364,255 C450,255 460,356 512,356" fill="none" stroke="#5c5c72" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="6 4" marker-end="url(#ah)"/>
              <text class="d-edge" x="458" y="306" text-anchor="middle" fill="#b25000" data-i18n="d.edge.slow2">still failing</text>

              <rect x="520" y="40" width="270" height="72" rx="14" fill="#e8f5e9" stroke="#2e7d32" stroke-width="2.5"/>
              <text class="d-label" x="655" y="70" text-anchor="middle" data-i18n="d.m1">gemini-2.5-flash</text>
              <text class="d-sub" x="655" y="90" text-anchor="middle" data-i18n="d.m1.sub">Google Vertex AI — primary</text>

              <rect x="520" y="180" width="270" height="72" rx="14" fill="#ffffff" stroke="rgba(26,26,46,0.28)" stroke-width="2"/>
              <text class="d-label" x="655" y="210" text-anchor="middle" data-i18n="d.m2">ChatGPT Realtime Mini 2.1</text>
              <text class="d-sub" x="655" y="230" text-anchor="middle" data-i18n="d.m2.sub">OpenAI — fallback 1</text>

              <rect x="520" y="320" width="270" height="72" rx="14" fill="#ffffff" stroke="rgba(26,26,46,0.28)" stroke-width="2"/>
              <text class="d-label" x="655" y="350" text-anchor="middle" data-i18n="d.m3">ChatGPT Realtime Mini</text>
              <text class="d-sub" x="655" y="370" text-anchor="middle" data-i18n="d.m3.sub">OpenAI — fallback 2</text>

              <path d="M790,356 L852,356 L852,76 L798,76" fill="none" stroke="#2e7d32" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-dasharray="7 5" marker-end="url(#ah-green)"/>
              <text class="d-edge" x="872" y="216" text-anchor="middle" fill="#2e7d32" transform="rotate(-90 872 216)" data-i18n="d.edge.recover">retried at intervals</text>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <p class="diagram-caption" data-i18n="diagram.caption">All three connections on the right carry your voice directly from the game to the provider. The connection to our server carries only the token.</p>

          <ol class="steps">
            <li><span class="n">1</span><span data-i18n="step.1">Before a conversation starts, the game asks our server to confirm that you own the game. Our server returns a short-lived token and nothing else. Your voice never passes through it.</span></li>
            <li><span class="n">2</span><span data-i18n="step.2">The game then connects straight to the provider and streams your voice there. gemini-2.5-flash on Vertex AI is used by default.</span></li>
            <li><span class="n">3</span><span data-i18n="step.3">If that connection becomes too slow or cannot be reached, the game switches to ChatGPT Realtime Mini 2.1, and to ChatGPT Realtime Mini if that one fails as well.</span></li>
            <li><span class="n">4</span><span data-i18n="step.4">At regular intervals the game retries the higher-priority service and moves back to it once it is healthy. A single play session can therefore use more than one provider.</span></li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section class="block" aria-labelledby="data-title">
          <h2 class="block-title" id="data-title" data-i18n="data.title">What is sent</h2>
          <p class="block-intro" data-i18n="data.intro">Whichever service is active receives the same thing: your voice, plus the small amount of game state needed to answer sensibly.</p>

          <div class="panel sent">
            <h3 data-i18n="sent.title">Sent to the provider</h3>
            <ul>
              <li data-i18n="sent.1">Your voice, streamed while a conversation is active.</li>
              <li data-i18n="sent.2">The current in-game situation, such as the driving scenario in progress.</li>
              <li data-i18n="sent.3">Recent turns of the same conversation, so replies stay coherent.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <p class="note" data-i18n="data.note">Your voice is never sent to our servers. It goes from the game straight to the provider, and our server is involved only long enough to confirm your purchase and hand back a token — which it keeps no record of.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="block" aria-labelledby="policy-title">
          <h2 class="block-title" id="policy-title" data-i18n="policy.title">What each provider does with it</h2>
          <p class="block-intro" data-i18n="policy.intro">Each provider sets its own terms for the data it receives. The summaries below are ours; the linked documents are authoritative.</p>

          <div class="table-scroll">
            <table class="policy">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="col" data-i18n="th.provider">Provider</th>
                  <th scope="col" data-i18n="th.training">Used to train models</th>
                  <th scope="col" data-i18n="th.retention">Retention</th>
                  <th scope="col" data-i18n="th.policy">Official documents</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">Google<br><span class="model-provider">Vertex AI<br>gemini-2.5-flash</span></th>
                  <td><span class="pill no" data-i18n="pill.no">No</span><br><span data-i18n="g.training">Google states it will not use your data to train or fine-tune its models without your permission, and that by default it does not use customer data to train its foundation models.</span></td>
                  <td data-i18n="g.retention">Governed by Google Cloud's data governance terms for Vertex AI. See the linked document for the current terms.</td>
                  <td>
                    <a href="https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/data-governance" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-i18n="g.link1">Vertex AI data governance</a><br>
                    <a href="https://cloud.google.com/terms/service-terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-i18n="g.link2">Google Cloud Service Specific Terms</a><br>
                    <a href="https://cloud.google.com/terms/cloud-privacy-notice" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-i18n="g.link3">Google Cloud Privacy Notice</a>
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row">OpenAI<br><span class="model-provider">Realtime API<br>ChatGPT Realtime Mini 2.1<br>ChatGPT Realtime Mini</span></th>
                  <td><span class="pill no" data-i18n="pill.no">No</span><br><span data-i18n="o.training">Data sent to the OpenAI API is not used to train or improve OpenAI models unless the customer explicitly opts in. We do not opt in.</span></td>
                  <td data-i18n="o.retention">For the Realtime endpoint, OpenAI keeps abuse-monitoring logs for up to 30 days unless a longer period is required by law, and stores no application state.</td>
                  <td>
                    <a href="https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/your-data" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-i18n="o.link1">How OpenAI handles your data</a><br>
                    <a href="https://openai.com/policies/privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-i18n="o.link2">OpenAI Privacy Policy</a><br>
                    <a href="https://openai.com/enterprise-privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-i18n="o.link3">OpenAI Enterprise Privacy</a>
                  </td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="block" aria-labelledby="guard-title">
          <h2 class="block-title" id="guard-title" data-i18n="guard.title">Guardrails on what the AI can say</h2>
          <p class="block-intro" data-i18n="guard.intro">Replies are generated live, so they are not written and checked in advance. These are the limits we put on them.</p>
          <ul class="steps" style="list-style: none;">
            <li><span class="n">1</span><span data-i18n="guard.1">System prompts keep the conversation on the subject of the game — coaching your younger sister through a driving lesson — and steer it back when it drifts.</span></li>
            <li><span class="n">2</span><span data-i18n="guard.2">Further prompts hold the in-game roles in place so the scene stays coherent and stays immersive.</span></li>
            <li><span class="n">3</span><span data-i18n="guard.3">If the game ever says something inappropriate, tell us on our Discord server and we will look into it.</span></li>
          </ul>
          <p><a href="https://discord.gg/FGKPcydtty" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-i18n="guard.discord">Report it on our Discord</a></p>
        </section>

        <section class="block" aria-labelledby="keep-title">
          <h2 class="block-title" id="keep-title" data-i18n="keep.title">What we keep</h2>
          <p class="block-intro" data-i18n="keep.intro">Separately from the providers, here is what Easy Fox Games holds.</p>
          <div class="split">
            <div class="panel kept">
              <h3 data-i18n="keep.noTitle">We do not keep</h3>
              <ul>
                <li data-i18n="keep.no1">Recordings of your voice. Your audio is not sent to us in the first place.</li>
                <li data-i18n="keep.no2">Any record of the play token we issue.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="panel sent">
              <h3 data-i18n="keep.yesTitle">We do keep</h3>
              <ul>
                <li data-i18n="keep.yes1">The replies the AI produces, read through the logging each provider offers inside our own account. We use them to improve the writing and the pacing of the game.</li>
                <li data-i18n="keep.yes2">Gameplay figures such as time spent per stage and number of failures — only if you agree when the game starts, and only to balance the difficulty.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="block" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
          <h2 class="block-title" id="contact-title" data-i18n="contact.title">Questions</h2>
          <p class="block-intro" data-i18n="contact.body">If anything on this page is unclear, or you have a question about how the game uses AI, get in touch — we are happy to help.</p>
          <p><a href="mailto:easyfoxgames@gmail.com">easyfoxgames@gmail.com</a></p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <nav class="footer-nav" aria-label="Footer">
        <a href="/" data-i18n="nav.home">Home</a>
